TODO — Workflow Orchestration Engine

Current foundation:
- [ ] ITask<TResult> with Id
- [ ] ITaskProcessor<TTask, TResult>
- [ ] Concrete processors exposed through non-generic processor types where useful
- [ ] Tasks are created by the caller; processors are resolved through DI
- [ ] No IResult so far

Revisit task composition:

- [ ] ConditionalTask
    - Needs to contain two tasks.
    - ITask<TResult> is generic, so decide how the two tasks are represented.
    - Decide whether both branches must produce the same TResult.
    - If different result types are allowed, determine how to represent that safely.
    - Avoid unnecessary runtime type switching / IResult unless justified.

- [ ] TransformTask
    - Takes the output of one task.
    - Transforms TSource → TResult.
    - Determine whether this should remain a concrete task or become a simpler composition operation.
    - Figure out how TransformTask interacts with ConditionalTask.
    - Ideally preserve compile-time type safety without manually specifying redundant types.

Main design goal:
- Keep task composition expressive and type-safe.
- Avoid the stiffness of the original Result / TransformTask / processor setup.

